[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68976,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mucinous tubular and spindle cell carcinoma is a renal epithelial neoplasm characterized by tubules merging with bland spindle cells and myxoid stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68977,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8480/3 Mucinous tubular and spindle cell carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68978,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C90.0 &amp; XH5EQ2 Renal cell carcinoma of kidney, except renal pelvis &amp; Mucinous tubular and spindle cell carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68979,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> low-grade collecting duct carcinoma; low-grade tubular-mucinous renal neoplasm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68980,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68981,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mucinous tubular and spindle cell carcinoma generally occurs in the renal cortex, but it may involve or arise within the renal medulla.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68982,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients are asymptomatic with an incidental renal mass {11381369; 25395040; 31151928}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68983,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mucinous tubular and spindle cell carcinoma accounts for &lt;&nbsp;1% of all renal neoplasms. There is a female predilection (M:F&nbsp;ratio: 1:3&ndash;4) and a broad age range (13&ndash;84&nbsp;years; median age in the sixth decade of life) {14660100; 25395040; 31151928}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68984,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68985,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are recurrent copy-number alterations and multiple chromosomal losses frequently involving chromosomes&nbsp;1, 4, 6, 8, 9, 13, 14, 15, and 22 {12429795; 27604489; 29462091; 26009022; 28656700; 32879414}. Biallelic dysregulation of the Hippo pathway tumour suppressor genes is common {27604489}. <em>CDKN2A</em> or <em>CDKN2B</em> deletion and additional complex genomic abnormalities may be present in high-grade tumours {32879414}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68986,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are mostly well-circumscribed masses with a solid, grey-white, tan, or yellow cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68987,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours classically consist of tightly packed, elongated, and anastomosing tubules lined by low-grade cuboidal cells merging with bland spindle cells in a myxoid stroma containing basophilic extracellular mucin. Various ratios of the elements result in spindle cell&ndash;dominant, epithelial-dominant, or mucin-poor morphology {17122511}. Tubules with tufting or small papillae and foci of foamy macrophages may occur, which can lead to morphological overlap with papillary renal cell carcinoma. Cells are low-grade with rare mitoses, and they may show clear cytoplasm or oncocytic changes. Immunohistochemically, tumours express PAX8, CK7, AMACR, and (rarely) CD10 {16330937; 17240302}.</p>\r\n<p>Tumours with high-grade transformation have high-grade nuclei, necrosis, increased mitoses, vascular invasion, and solid or infiltrative growth {18830937; 28656700; 32879414}. An expansile, high-grade spindle cell element is defined as sarcomatoid transformation {18941398}. Areas with classic histology may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68988,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FNA is typically cellular with aggregates of low-grade, uniform, oval to spindle cells intermixed with abundant metachromatic myxoid matrix {17703454; 19626627}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68989,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is multiple chromosomal loss by copy-number analysis, and <em>VSTM2A</em> RNA expression by in&nbsp;situ hybridization is an emerging diagnostic marker {30285995; 33239504}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68990,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> anastomosing tubules lined by low-grade cuboidal cells merging with bland spindle cells in a stroma with basophilic extracellular mucin.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> chromosomal loss by copy-number analyses in challenging cases or small biopsies.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68991,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Staging follows the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) and American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) staging systems.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 68992,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours with high-grade transformation are often associated with distant metastasis and death. Rare cases with classic morphology can also develop metastases {21194728; 21684183; 25395040; 31151928; 32675442}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T15:59:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]